{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"f74369e0-f2ed-48b3-a759-5aa42e975543","agentId":"a064032b3180b0755","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Repo C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers. Python .venv\\Scripts\\python.exe. No subagents, no COM3; TestClient only. Report under 60 words. Another agent is editing report_routes.py/report.html and the parts/faulttree bridges: do not touch those. You own cuore/web/templates/fullscan.html, static/fullscan.css, cuore/web/fullscan_routes.py (context only), docs/handbook/07-first-live-session.md (additive), cuore/tests/check_fullscan.py (extend). You may commit and push (`github` main only; never koch-mcp/).\n\nAdd a \"Which cable for which module\" reference, generated from the live module table (cuore/live/buses.py + the module registry ops.modules() reads; never hand-typed): on the Full scan wizard idle screen and on each pause card, a compact three-column block — Standard plug (CAN-C): ECM, TCM, BCM, IPC, RFHUB, DTCM, ESM, DASM · Blue A5 (CAN-IHS): HVAC, ETM, AMP, ESEM, CSWM, CRSM, LBSS, RBSS, PLGM · Grey A6 (CAN-CH): ABS, EPS, ORC, AFLS, PAM, HALF, TVM, ESL — with each module's confidence chip (confirmed / unverified / inferred / unknown) from the table and the adapter switch note (HS for the standard plug and grey; MS for blue) sourced from buses.py's route notes. The same table goes into the handbook section as markdown generated by a tiny script you add under docs/handbook/ (so it never drifts: cuore/tests/check_fullscan.py asserts the rendered wizard block lists every module the table has, per bus). Shop-floor rules, nothing under 12px. Commit \"Full scan: which cable for which module, generated from the module table\" with the Co-Authored-By line, push, report the hash."},"uuid":"2205ef35-ee32-4fef-b6ca-bb4d0ceaee94","timestamp":"2026-10-14T05:28:41.310Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282",