{"parentUuid":"cf6f32bb-9314-4287-b407-6e85ab5ae68f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"18814b70-8b7e-4c43-946c-5c9dac496990","agentId":"a064032b3180b0755","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NEC37dET2RjdNGPtaqqHuB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"``/v/{vin}/scan`` -- the guided full-scan wizard.\n2\t\n3\tThe garage's bypass cables have to be swapped by hand mid-scan (blue A5 for\n4\tCAN-IHS, grey A6 for CAN-CH); this page is what makes that feel like one\n5\tcontinuous scan instead of three separate ones the mechanic has to restart.\n6\tEvery actual read, every bit of state, and the whole pause/resume machinery\n7\tlive in :mod:`cuore.live.fullscan` (``run_guided``/``continue_guided``/\n8\t``skip_guided``/``abandon_guided``) -- this module only renders that state\n9\tand relays the four actions as plain form posts.\n10\t\n11\tSame posture as ``cuore/web/tests_routes.py``/``cuore/web/scan_health_routes.py``:\n12\ta second router over ``cuore.web.routes``'s own ``_page``/``_dossier``/\n13\t``_vehicle_bar`` helpers, so this page looks and behaves like every other\n14\t``/v/{vin}`` page (same vehicle bar, same tab strip, same error handling --\n15\ta ``BridgeError`` raised from ``fullscan.py`` is rendered by ``cuore.app``'s\n16\town exception handler exactly as it is everywhere else).\n17\t\n18\tWorks without JS: every POST here is a plain ``<form>`` that redirects\n19\t(303) straight back to the GET page, which always renders whatever phase\n20\tthe persisted guided-scan state says it's in. ``cuore/web/static/fullscan.js``\n21\tonly adds a \"Working...\" busy state on the button that is about to block for\n22\ta real adapter read, and a 1.5s poll of the state endpoint while a pause\n23\tcard is showing (so this screen notices if the MCP tools or a second tab\n24\tmoved the same session on, and reloads to match) -- neither changes what\n25\tgets POSTed or rendered.\n26\t\"\"\"\n27\t\n28\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n29\t\n30\tfrom typing import Any\n31\t\n32\tfrom fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, Form, Request\n33\tfrom fastapi.responses import HTMLResponse, RedirectResponse\n34\t\n35\tfrom ..api.deps import require_token\n36\tfrom ..live import buses as live_buses\n37\tfrom ..live import fullscan\n38\tfrom ..live import ops as live_ops\n39\tfrom ..services import shop_bridge\n40\tfrom .routes import _dossier, _page, _set_active_vehicle, _vehicle_bar\n41\t\n42\t#: Server-rendered page: same posture as cuore.web.routes.router and\n43\t#: cuore.web.tests_routes.router.\n44\trouter = APIRouter(include_in_schema=False, dependencies=[Depends(require_token)])\n45\t\n46\t#: Presentation-only labels for the three cable states. Never a source of\n47\t#: which module goes under which cable -- that comes from cable_reference_table()\n48\t#: below, generated straight from cuore.live.buses + cuore.live.ops.modules().\n49\t_CABLE_LABELS = {\"none\": \"Standard plug\", \"blue_a5\": \"Blue A5\", \"grey_a6\": \"Grey A6\"}\n50\t_CABLE_ORDER = {\"none\": 0, \"blue_a5\": 1, \"grey_a6\": 2}\n51\t\n52\t\n53\tdef cable_reference_table() -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n54\t    \"\"\"\"Which cable for which module\" data, generated fresh every call.\n55\t\n56\t    Never hand-typed: the bus/cable pairing and the HS/MS adapter-switch\n57\t    note come straight from ``cuore.live.buses`` (each ``Bus``'s own routes\n58\t    and bitrate -- the bypass-cable route, where one exists, over the\n59\t    no-cable alternate; HS for a 500k/HS-CAN bus, MS for a 125k/MS-CAN one,\n60\t    per the \"MS-CAN transceiver\" wording in CAN_IHS's own route note), and"}]},"uuid":"264c920a-e1a5-409a-b02c-9eab0cad911c","timestamp":"2026-10-14T05:33:59.346Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\cuore\\web\\fullscan_routes.py","content":"\"\"\"``/v/{vin}/scan`` -- the guided full-scan wizard.\n\nThe garage's bypass cables have to be swapped by hand mid-scan (blue A5 for\nCAN-IHS, grey A6 for CAN-CH); this page is what makes that feel like one\ncontinuous scan instead of three separate ones the mechanic has to restart.\nEvery actual read, every bit of state, and the whole pause/resume machinery\nlive in :mod:`cuore.live.fullscan` (``run_guided``/``continue_guided``/\n``skip_guided``/``abandon_guided``) -- this module only renders that state\nand relays the four actions as plain form posts.\n\nSame posture as ``cuore/web/tests_routes.py``/``cuore/web/scan_health_routes.py``:\na second router over ``cuore.web.routes``'s own ``_page``/``_dossier``/\n``_vehicle_bar`` helpers, so this page looks and behaves like every other\n``/v/{vin}`` page (same vehicle bar, same tab strip, same error handling --\na ``BridgeError`` raised from ``fullscan.py`` is rendered by ``cuore.app``'s\nown exception handler exactly as it is everywhere else).\n\nWorks without JS: every POST here is a plain ``<form>`` that redirects\n(303) straight back to the GET page, which always renders whatever phase\nthe persisted guided-scan state says it's in. ``cuore/web/static/fullscan.js``\nonly adds a \"Working...\" busy state on the button that is about to block for\na real adapter read, and a 1.5s poll of the state endpoint while a pause\ncard is showing (so this screen notices if the MCP tools or a second tab\nmoved the same session on, and reloads to match) -- neither changes what\ngets POSTed or rendered.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, Depends, Form, Request\nfrom fastapi.responses import HTMLResponse, RedirectResponse\n\nfrom ..api.deps import require_token\nfrom ..live import buses as live_buses\nfrom ..live import fullscan\nfrom ..live import ops as live_ops\nfrom ..services import shop_bridge\nfrom .routes import _dossier, _page, _set_active_vehicle, _vehicle_bar\n\n#: Server-rendered page: same posture as cuore.web.routes.router and\n#: cuore.web.tests_routes.router.\nrouter = APIRouter(include_in_schema=False, dependencies=[Depends(require_token)])\n\n#: Presentation-only labels for the three cable states. Never a source of\n#: which module goes under which cable -- that comes from cable_reference_table()\n#: below, generated straight from cuore.live.buses + cuore.live.ops.modules().\n_CABLE_LABELS = {\"none\": \"Standard plug\", \"blue_a5\": \"Blue A5\", \"grey_a6\": \"Grey A6\"}\n_CABLE_ORDER = {\"none\": 0, \"blue_a5\": 1, \"grey_a6\": 2}\n\n\ndef cable_reference_table() -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\n    \"\"\"\"Which cable for which module\" data, generated fresh every call.\n\n    Never hand-typed: the bus/cable pairing and the HS/MS adapter-switch\n    note come straight from ``cuore.live.buses`` (each ``Bus``'s own routes\n    and bitrate -- the bypass-cable route, where one exists, over the\n    no-cable alternate; HS for a 500k/HS-CAN bus, MS for a 125k/MS-CAN one,\n    per the \"MS-CAN transceiver\" wording in CAN_IHS's own route note), and","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":162}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cf6f32bb-9314-4287-b407-6e85ab5ae68f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
