{"parentUuid":"cf3fb4ff-4534-45fe-a80c-bb6e8323bba4","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a064032b3180b0755","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011Cg1awQmBqGatWSiH1y1nc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BR9qG5XZqS78Uf14GiSL1x","name":"Bash","input":{"command":".venv/Scripts/python.exe docs/handbook/generate_cable_reference.py && tail -n 60 docs/handbook/07-first-live-session.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1391,"cache_read_input_tokens":142383,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1391,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BR9qG5XZqS78Uf14GiSL1x":{"command":"cd C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers && .venv/Scripts/python.exe docs/handbook/generate_cable_reference.py && tail -n 60 docs/handbook/07-first-live-session.md"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01BR9qG5XZqS78Uf14GiSL1x":{"cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"53e49779-1d7e-45a4-94f6-6c4b5f56eb4b","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cg1awQWK9tHYw5g6U6tDd","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"44dc9f58-3a26-4ca6-a215-14119566b72d","timestamp":"2026-10-14T05:34:58.144Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers","sessionId":"7cb02eb5-e299-4baf-b34b-9eb82aebbf17","version":"2.1.282","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"binary-splashing-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"44dc9f58-3a26-4ca6-a215-14119566b72d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"18814b70-8b7e-4c43-946c-5c9dac496990","agentId":"a064032b3180b0755","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BR9qG5XZqS78Uf14GiSL1x","type":"tool_result","content":"wrote C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\handbook\\07-first-live-session.md\r\na page action (`POST /api/buscapture/{bus}/learn/accept`), not an MCP\r\ntool.\r\n\r\n**Per-bus presets** -- `chassis_a6` (CAN-CH: ABS wheel speeds, steering\r\nangle, yaw rate) and `body_a5` (CAN-IHS: HVAC temperature, battery\r\nmonitor, door states) list only what a public broadcast-signal source\r\n(`cuore.live.did_catalog.BROADCAST_SIGNALS`) or this VIN's own learned\r\nsignals actually cover; anything else is shown `unknown_did` and is never\r\npolled or implied to exist (brake pressure, for example, has no known\r\nbroadcast signal or DID on this platform and always shows `unknown_did`\r\nin `chassis_a6`). The Live board shows each preset's required cable and\r\nrefuses to start it (`Refused`) without that cable declared.\r\n\r\n<!-- cable-reference:start (generated by docs/handbook/generate_cable_reference.py -- do not hand-edit between these markers; re-run the script instead) -->\r\n\r\n## 8. Which cable for which module\r\n\r\nGenerated straight from the live module registry (`cuore/live/buses.py` + `cuore.live.ops.modules()`) by `docs/handbook/generate_cable_reference.py` -- never hand-typed. This is the same table the Full scan wizard (`/v/{vin}/scan`) shows on its idle screen and on every pause card, so the page and this section can never disagree with each other or with the registry both are drawn from. Re-run the script after any change to `addressing.py` or `buses.py`.\r\n\r\n### Standard plug (CAN-C) -- adapter switch: HS\r\n\r\n| Module | Confidence |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| ECM | confirmed |\r\n| TCM | confirmed |\r\n| BCM | confirmed |\r\n| IPC | confirmed |\r\n| RFHUB | confirmed |\r\n| DTCM | unverified |\r\n| ESM | unknown |\r\n| DASM | unknown |\r\n\r\n### Blue A5 (CAN-IHS) -- adapter switch: MS\r\n\r\n| Module | Confidence |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| HVAC | unverified |\r\n| ETM | unverified |\r\n| AMP | unknown |\r\n| ESEM | unknown |\r\n| CSWM | unknown |\r\n| CRSM | unknown |\r\n| LBSS | unknown |\r\n| RBSS | unknown |\r\n| PLGM | unknown |\r\n\r\n### Grey A6 (CAN-CH) -- adapter switch: HS\r\n\r\n| Module | Confidence |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| ABS | unverified |\r\n| EPS | inferred |\r\n| ORC | unverified |\r\n| AFLS | unknown |\r\n| PAM | unknown |\r\n| HALF | unknown |\r\n| TVM | unknown |\r\n| ESL | unknown |\r\n\r\n<!-- cable-reference:end -->","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f2906ad9-2bda-47f6-8cd1-361fbf6d2ccf","timestamp":"2026-10-14T05:35:01.889Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"wrote C:\\Users\\User\\mcp-servers\\docs\\handbook\\07-first-live-session.md\r\na page action (`POST /api/buscapture/{bus}/learn/accept`), not an MCP\r\ntool.\r\n\r\n**Per-bus presets** -- `chassis_a6` (CAN-CH: ABS wheel speeds, steering\r\nangle, yaw rate) and `body_a5` (CAN-IHS: HVAC temperature, battery\r\nmonitor, door states) list only what a public broadcast-signal source\r\n(`cuore.live.did_catalog.BROADCAST_SIGNALS`) or this VIN's own learned\r\nsignals actually cover; anything else is shown `unknown_did` and is never\r\npolled or implied to exist (brake pressure, for example, has no known\r\nbroadcast signal or DID on this platform and always shows `unknown_did`\r\nin `chassis_a6`). The Live board shows each preset's required cable and\r\nrefuses to start it (`Refused`) without that cable declared.\r\n\r\n<!-- cable-reference:start (generated by docs/handbook/generate_cable_reference.py -- do not hand-edit between these markers; re-run the script instead) -->\r\n\r\n## 8. Which cable for which module\r\n\r\nGenerated straight from the live module registry (`cuore/live/buses.py` + `cuore.live.ops.modules()`) by `docs/handbook/generate_cable_reference.py` -- never hand-typed. This i